.TH CCOL_CREATE_CHTTPCLIENT_MP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_create_chttpclient_mp \- create an HTTP client with a custom allocator
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

chttpcli ccol_create_chttpclient_mp(ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mprocs,
                               char **err_str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function allocates and initializes a new HTTP client. It does NOT
create the connection pool yet: the library initializes that pool on
the first request.

The default configuration after the creation is:
  pool size              = the CPU count (resolved on the first
                           request)
  connect timeout        = 0 (no timeout)
  request timeout        = 0 (no timeout)
  max response body size = 0 (no limit)
  TLS                    = peer and host verification on,
                           system CA
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
mprocs    A custom allocator, or NULL for malloc/free.
err_str   Optional. It gets a static error string if the call fails.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A new client handle, or CHTTPCLI_INVALID if the call fails.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_create_chttpclient (3),
.BR chttpclient_destroy (3),
.BR chttpclient_set_pool_size (3)
